# Fixture generation and provenance

- Generate fixtures using exact pinned binaries.
- Use isolated temporary homes and stores.
- Generate lockfile bytes and metadata in the same real invocation.
- Do not manually edit provenance metadata after generation.
- Keep generation and verification as separate operations.
- Verification must be read-only.
- Regenerated lockfiles, manifests, workspace files, patches, and metadata must be committed together.

Fixture metadata should record: producer; exact producer version; producer major; Node version; operating system; architecture; exact executable command; exact arguments; registry; source family; timestamp; generated, derived, or curated classification; lockfile version; lockfile SHA-256; package manifest SHA-256; workspace manifest SHA-256 when present; workspace package manifest hashes; patch file hashes; source-tree digest; generation invocation identifier.

Derived Nub fixtures must also record: exact source pnpm fixture; exact source lockfile hash; source manifest hashes; derivation command; resulting Nub lock hash; `derived` classification.

The verifier must reject: placeholder commands; manually invented provenance descriptions; pin mismatches; lock hash mismatches; source manifest mismatches; workspace manifest mismatches; patch hash mismatches; missing source digest; missing derived-source hash; incorrect classification; missing registry; missing generation identifier; stale metadata.
<!-- MEW-FIXTURES_END -->
